      "id": "claim_4846836fc1494ae981ffa8c3556745ee",
      "statement": "Ugoira zip downloads keep the shared OkHttp budget (a multi-MB zip legitimately takes budget-sized time on a slow-but-stable mirror) and may only switch to the official URL before the byte stream is handed to its consumer; once frames are being read, a mid-stream source switch is forbidden because already-delivered frames would come from the mirror while continued reads came from the official host, breaking the ZIP entry stream's continuity — a boundary pinned by `PictelioApiModuleTest.streamDownloadZip_mirrorMidStreamFailure_noSourceSwitch`.",
